<title>FRANCE: UAP sharply down ahead of H1 results.</title>
<headline>UAP sharply down ahead of H1 results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Union des Assurances de Paris were down 2.9 percent in midday trading on the bourse on investor nervousness ahead of the insurance group's first-half results due on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The stock was down 3.30 francs at 109.10 at 1000 GMT.</p>
<p>Analysts expect a fall in first-half profit to 750-800 million francs from 806 million last year.</p>
<p>&quot;It's had a great rally, a lot due to (takeover) speculation between UAP and Axa, but there's a bit of nervousness ahead of the results,&quot; a broker said. Volume was 513,736 shares.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
